  "rationale": "The structural obligations are met.\n\n**1. The trait method.** The requirement asks for `SourceProvider: Send + Sync` with `type Error: From<SourceError> + Send`. It also asks for `fn list(&self, scope: &SourceScope) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Vec<ResourceId>, Self::Error>> + Send`. `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]` declares exactly this, including the supertraits and the associated `Error` bound. `crates/habeas-sdk/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]/fn[list]` has the required signature and is marked `{impl}`. The trait's other methods (`read`, `parse`, `search_text`, `search_structure`) fit the \"other provider methods omitted\" comment.\n\n**2. The source tools expose the `list_sources` command through the application's provider.**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<'_, P, F, D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` registers a `list_sources` tool definition with an optional `prefix` parameter.\n- `fn[dispatch]` in the same impl handles the `\"list_sources\"` case. It takes `provider = &self.tools.analysis.provider` and calls `provider.list(&scope).await`. It serializes the resulting `Vec<ResourceId>` and converts a provider error into an `io::Error`. The provider is the generic one the application supplies.\n\nThe tool's inputs and behavior belong to the refining `list_sources.inputs` and `list_sources.behavior` declarations. This assessment does not cover them.\n\nNo gaps and no ambiguities were found, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
